<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Analyze Percent Change Over Time</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01208</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Analyze Percent Change Over Time</md:title>
    <md:uuid>528a9146-fe33-4570-9e21-5c30e4686d63</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><blockquote>A cell phone is plugged in to be charged. The table below shows the percent of battery power at a few times after it was plugged in. Use the data to find out. Be prepared to show your reasoning.</blockquote>

<table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis>Time</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Percentage Charged</emphasis></entry></row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>11:00 a.m.</entry>
      <entry>6%</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>11:10 a.m.</entry>
      <entry>15%</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>11:30 a.m.</entry>
      <entry>35%</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>11:40 a.m.</entry>
      <entry>43%</entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<list type="enumerated"><item>At what time will the battery be 100% charged?</item></list></section>
</content>
</document>
